# Density Compare
# Selenium (Se) — real density 4.81 g/cm³. equal masses: Selenium vs water — sides ∝ (1/ρ)^(1/3).
scene "Selenium Density Compare"

element_cube = cube 11.8mm color: #ffa100 at (-20mm, 5.9mm, 0)
water_cube = cube 20mm material: water at (18mm, 10mm, 0)
# both cubes weigh the same: about 38.4 g — the water cube is the reference
